WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

2
00:02:16.843 --> 00:02:18.345
Tully's been here.

3
00:02:19.721 --> 00:02:22.307
We found one of their camps just ahead.

4
00:02:23.558 --> 00:02:26.561
But something strange has happened there.

5
00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:06.268
They're all Rivermen.

6
00:03:08.353 --> 00:03:09.396
Who killed them?

7
00:03:10.647 --> 00:03:12.357
We found no sign of their foe.

8
00:03:29.958 --> 00:03:31.543
They did not fall here.

9
00:03:38.008 --> 00:03:39.676
On your guard!

10
00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:41.470
It's a trap!

11
00:03:56.067 --> 00:03:57.235
To me!

12
00:05:10.767 --> 00:05:12.269
We light the way!

13
00:05:12.352 --> 00:05:15.313
We light the way!

14
00:05:34.374 --> 00:05:35.625
This was not the battle.

15
00:05:43.049 --> 00:05:44.885
Who are they?

16
00:05:46.011 --> 00:05:47.470
Our death.

17
00:05:51.016 --> 00:05:52.517
Criston Cole!

18
00:05:54.728 --> 00:05:59.065
Traitor. usurper. and defiler of justice.

19
00:05:59.149 --> 00:06:00.942
Come forth to hear your fate.

20
00:06:01.568 --> 00:06:04.613
If I strike my banners.
will you spare my men their lives?

21
00:06:05.447 --> 00:06:08.033
I made a promise to the dead. Cole.

22
00:06:08.116 --> 00:06:10.702
I told them I'd build a sept
out of traitors' bones.

23
00:06:11.578 --> 00:06:13.246
I don't have near enough bones yet.

24
00:06:21.922 --> 00:06:24.716
If there is to be battle here.
many of you will die as well.

25
00:06:25.342 --> 00:06:26.760
That's why we've come.

26
00:06:26.843 --> 00:06:30.680
What better way to die than blade in hand?

27
00:06:34.976 --> 00:06:36.394
As you will it.

28
00:06:55.747 --> 00:06:57.582
Let us begin here then.

29
00:06:59.542 --> 00:07:01.336
One of me against the two of you.

30
00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:06.466
Will that be enough to make a fight of it?

31
00:08:07.318 --> 00:08:08.611
They're here.

32
00:08:19.497 --> 00:08:22.500
I mourn my friend Ser Luthor.

33
00:08:22.584 --> 00:08:25.170
and some four and 10 of his best men.

34
00:08:25.253 --> 00:08:26.838
A total count of five and 20
of the City Watch

35
00:08:26.921 --> 00:08:28.757
now slain in the name of "King Daeron."

36
00:08:29.758 --> 00:08:33.178
Lord Ormund mocks us in our own city.

37
00:08:33.261 --> 00:08:37.557
He means to show the realm
that I cannot govern even my own seat.

38
00:08:38.183 --> 00:08:41.311
The great houses watch
while he humiliates me.

39
00:08:41.394 --> 00:08:42.562
Where is my army?

40
00:08:43.313 --> 00:08:45.023
Ser Criston has hindered them.

41
00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:48.985
The vanguard is still a fortnight's march
from Tumbleton.

42
00:08:49.069 --> 00:08:50.361
The insult must be answered now.

43
00:08:50.445 --> 00:08:51.738
We must do what we should
have done in the first.

44
00:08:51.821 --> 00:08:53.406
Burn the villains out.

45
00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:55.158
Then Ormund gets what he wants.

46
00:08:55.784 --> 00:08:58.661
A queen who murders loyal subjects
cannot be trusted.

47
00:08:58.745 --> 00:09:00.538
We know where the traitor
has entrenched himself.

48
00:09:00.622 --> 00:09:03.208
If I fly directly
to the Footly stronghold--

49
00:09:03.291 --> 00:09:05.043
On a dragon. I presume.

50
00:09:05.126 --> 00:09:09.005
A beast well known for its delicacy
and precision in battle.

51
00:09:09.089 --> 00:09:10.882
Ah. yes. what a marvel.

52
00:09:10.965 --> 00:09:13.468
The flame it spews forth
can discern with pure magic

53
00:09:13.551 --> 00:09:15.136
who is blameless and who is deserving--

54
00:09:17.347 --> 00:09:19.432
I'll hear no more from those
whose greatest battle

55
00:09:19.516 --> 00:09:20.767
has been with their own indigestion.

56
00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:24.896
I am of the same mind as the lord
and ladies. Your Grace.

57
00:09:24.979 --> 00:09:27.065
Your army marches ever nearer.

58
00:09:28.525 --> 00:09:30.902
You will answer this outrage with force

59
00:09:30.985 --> 00:09:33.071
but discriminately...

60
00:09:35.865 --> 00:09:37.826
- ...if we wait but a while longer.
- At what cost?

61
00:09:38.993 --> 00:09:41.121
Remember the prophecy.
your sacred calling.

62
00:09:41.204 --> 00:09:43.581
Whatever you do in its service
is justified.

63
00:09:43.665 --> 00:09:46.668
Aegon the Conqueror burned thousands
on the Field of Fire. thousands.

64
00:09:46.751 --> 00:09:48.002
and settled the realm for generations--

65
00:09:48.086 --> 00:09:49.379
The Conqueror

66
00:09:49.462 --> 00:09:51.381
burned enemy soldiers.
not subjects who bent the knee.

67
00:09:51.464 --> 00:09:53.508
Their lord bent the knee to you!

68
00:09:54.551 --> 00:09:56.386
The people would just as happily
follow a mule

69
00:09:56.469 --> 00:09:58.304
- if that same--
- My father would abhor it.

70
00:09:58.388 --> 00:10:00.223
Ah. and there we have it.

71
00:10:01.933 --> 00:10:02.934
But...

72
00:10:04.144 --> 00:10:06.604
my patience has its bounds.

73
00:10:06.688 --> 00:10:08.606
- I will send knives.
- So be it.

74
00:10:08.690 --> 00:10:11.151
At least I will get to meet
the fiend face-to-face before he dies.

75
00:10:11.234 --> 00:10:12.318
Oh. no. not you.

76
00:10:14.529 --> 00:10:16.114
I will have my satisfaction.

77
00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:18.783
Yes.

78
00:10:19.701 --> 00:10:21.953
But the most effective assassin
has a plain face.

79
00:10:23.663 --> 00:10:25.874
Fanatics still prowl the streets

80
00:10:25.957 --> 00:10:28.751
outside our castle gates
at Lord Ormund's bidding.

81
00:10:28.835 --> 00:10:30.545
That is your charge.

82
00:10:34.132 --> 00:10:37.260
Your Grace. there is a detachment
left here of Velaryon men. soldiers.

83
00:10:37.343 --> 00:10:39.095
ready to aid Prince Daemon in his--

84
00:10:39.179 --> 00:10:40.513
I think not.

85
00:10:45.101 --> 00:10:48.730
How many Velaryon men
remain in King's Landing?

86
00:10:48.813 --> 00:10:50.398
Some threescore. Your Grace.

87
00:10:50.481 --> 00:10:52.400
Petition your father for more.

88
00:10:52.483 --> 00:10:54.736
They may be needed to secure the city.

89
00:10:54.819 --> 00:10:56.988
Who then will you send to Tumbleton?

90
00:10:57.989 --> 00:11:01.576
It is a dangerous errand.
and one that will require force.

91
00:11:03.494 --> 00:11:06.915
My queen. the delegation
from House Baratheon has arrived.

92
00:11:08.958 --> 00:11:13.171
Your Grace. I am sent
to represent House Baratheon

93
00:11:13.254 --> 00:11:14.589
in response to your summons.

94
00:11:16.883 --> 00:11:18.092
Where is Lord Borros?

95
00:11:18.176 --> 00:11:20.386
Lord Borros begs patience. my queen.

96
00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:23.848
He has taken his army to the Red Mountains
to fight the Vulture King.

97
00:11:23.932 --> 00:11:26.726
who has been raiding the Stormlands
these many moons.

98
00:11:26.809 --> 00:11:28.811
His queen summons him north.

99
00:11:28.895 --> 00:11:31.814
and all of a sudden it occurs to him
that he must ride south.

100
00:11:33.066 --> 00:11:35.109
It is my lord's duty

101
00:11:35.193 --> 00:11:37.445
to guard the realm
against the Dornish threat.

102
00:11:37.528 --> 00:11:39.280
As it was his duty to guard my son

103
00:11:39.364 --> 00:11:41.824
when he came to treat
with him beneath his roof?

104
00:11:43.076 --> 00:11:45.036
Once the Vulture King has been subdued--

105
00:11:45.119 --> 00:11:47.914
Your lord makes the mistake
of considering a common bandit

106
00:11:47.997 --> 00:11:50.708
a greater threat
to his interests than I am.

107
00:11:53.461 --> 00:11:57.048
I could brand him a traitor
and hang you in his stead.

108
00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:04.013
No disrespect was intended. Your Grace.
to you or your endeavors.

109
00:12:04.097 --> 00:12:05.348
It is but...

110
00:12:05.431 --> 00:12:06.766
but a matter of time.

111
00:12:06.849 --> 00:12:08.142
Time?

112
00:12:08.768 --> 00:12:12.397
If there were aught else I could offer you
at this moment.

113
00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:14.607
I would lay it before you most willingly.

114
00:12:20.571 --> 00:12:21.864
Give me your belt.

115
00:12:54.397 --> 00:12:55.523
Anything to report?

116
00:13:01.821 --> 00:13:03.156
Market day tomorrow.

117
00:13:03.239 --> 00:13:04.907
Do you remember Market Day
in King's Landing?

118
00:13:06.743 --> 00:13:07.910
Before all of this?

119
00:13:11.372 --> 00:13:12.665
Fruit stalls.

120
00:13:14.334 --> 00:13:16.502
Geese honking. Traders shouting.

121
00:13:18.671 --> 00:13:19.714
Hot pies.

122
00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:24.510
Took it all for granted. didn't we?

123
00:13:25.428 --> 00:13:27.305
It will soon be the same again. I imagine.

124
00:13:28.014 --> 00:13:30.058
But we're not the same. are we?

125
00:13:30.141 --> 00:13:31.976
We weren't in service back then.

126
00:13:33.686 --> 00:13:36.939
At the beck and call of the queen
sleeping on a hill.

127
00:13:37.940 --> 00:13:38.775
alone.

128
00:13:40.902 --> 00:13:43.237
She stopped me going to the tavern. Hugh.

129
00:13:43.321 --> 00:13:45.031
Not one ale with the lads.

130
00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:48.868
What's the point in having a dragon
if no one's around to see it?

131
00:13:51.412 --> 00:13:53.623
Well. would you go back to where you were?

132
00:13:53.706 --> 00:13:55.708
Scrabbling around in the dust?

133
00:13:57.293 --> 00:13:58.419
No.

134
00:14:01.631 --> 00:14:03.925
Though I can't say my life
has been improved.

135
00:14:06.135 --> 00:14:07.303
Can you?

136
00:14:13.518 --> 00:14:14.352
Right. then.

137
00:14:22.318 --> 00:14:23.694
See you in two days.

138
00:14:25.446 --> 00:14:26.697
Ser Hugh.

139
00:14:30.451 --> 00:14:31.327
Come on. girl.

140
00:14:46.926 --> 00:14:48.094
Leave us.

141
00:14:53.808 --> 00:14:54.976
You would have done the same.

142
00:14:56.269 --> 00:14:58.646
Have I not shown you mercy

143
00:14:58.729 --> 00:15:02.567
even before those who named
my kindness to you a weakness?

144
00:15:02.650 --> 00:15:04.402
Are you so ungrateful

145
00:15:04.485 --> 00:15:06.654
- that you insist upon--
- Helaena is with child.

146
00:15:11.617 --> 00:15:13.911
So. you flee.

147
00:15:14.787 --> 00:15:17.540
To preserve the babe's life.
and Helaena's with it.

148
00:15:17.623 --> 00:15:20.001
Still you insist on misjudging me.

149
00:15:21.085 --> 00:15:23.171
If the child is male.

150
00:15:23.254 --> 00:15:25.089
would you not in the end
find it necessary?

151
00:15:27.592 --> 00:15:29.218
To hold him hostage. at the least?

152
00:15:30.803 --> 00:15:32.346
To draw out Aemond or...

153
00:15:33.222 --> 00:15:34.765
or Ormund in his pride?

154
00:15:36.642 --> 00:15:39.896
Or simply to secure your own reign
from endless challenges.

155
00:15:39.979 --> 00:15:42.023
You were discovered by guards.

156
00:15:45.026 --> 00:15:47.195
I cannot let this go unanswered.

157
00:15:47.278 --> 00:15:48.863
Helaena did as I persuaded her to do.

158
00:15:48.946 --> 00:15:51.115
If you must be cruel.
let it be me who suffers.

159
00:15:51.199 --> 00:15:52.366
Only spare her.

160
00:15:53.493 --> 00:15:55.495
You must both now
be more strictly confined.

161
00:15:56.287 --> 00:15:58.080
Your guard is doubled.

162
00:15:58.164 --> 00:16:00.416
There'll be no more walks in the Godswood.

163
00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:02.210
- I accept this judgment for myself--
- My judgment

164
00:16:02.293 --> 00:16:04.003
does not require your acceptance.

165
00:16:04.086 --> 00:16:05.796
Rhaenyra. you know what she is.

166
00:16:05.880 --> 00:16:08.090
She is fragile. you cannot confine her.

167
00:16:08.174 --> 00:16:09.717
I didn't!

168
00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:11.719
And now. I must!

169
00:16:12.970 --> 00:16:14.972
She cannot be seen.

170
00:16:15.056 --> 00:16:18.434
If she is known to carry Aegon's heir.
I will be forced to do what you fear.

171
00:16:18.518 --> 00:16:21.062
Well. so. so. so send us away
then to some remote--

172
00:16:21.145 --> 00:16:23.439
Away? Now?

173
00:16:24.774 --> 00:16:26.067
Your son is still at liberty.

174
00:16:26.150 --> 00:16:28.778
Your cousin wreaks chaos
within my city walls.

175
00:16:30.196 --> 00:16:32.990
Even today. I must answer another
of his murderous treasons.

176
00:16:35.284 --> 00:16:38.746
You are a Hightower.
To my court. you are the enemy.

177
00:16:39.705 --> 00:16:40.873
And to you?

178
00:16:43.376 --> 00:16:44.585
Do not try me.

179
00:16:50.967 --> 00:16:52.468
What did she tell you?

180
00:16:53.844 --> 00:16:55.596
Helaena is with child.

181
00:16:57.974 --> 00:16:59.684
Are there others who know?

182
00:17:01.060 --> 00:17:02.436
I believe not.

183
00:17:03.354 --> 00:17:04.897
You yourself had no suspicion?

184
00:17:05.815 --> 00:17:06.816
No.

185
00:17:08.067 --> 00:17:09.110
No.

186
00:17:20.162 --> 00:17:21.831
That one.

187
00:17:21.914 --> 00:17:23.874
A thief and a liar.

188
00:17:25.876 --> 00:17:27.503
Let me know when it's done.

189
00:17:44.979 --> 00:17:46.522
We will be avenged.

190
00:17:49.025 --> 00:17:50.860
If it takes a hundred years.

191
00:18:00.911 --> 00:18:02.204
What's this?

192
00:18:05.750 --> 00:18:08.002
Forgive me. my prince.

193
00:18:08.085 --> 00:18:09.754
This is how you answer?

194
00:18:11.672 --> 00:18:12.715
With desertion?

195
00:18:12.798 --> 00:18:14.967
The queen asked for loyalty.

196
00:18:15.051 --> 00:18:16.886
and I was willing enough to wait.

197
00:18:18.387 --> 00:18:20.598
But my children are now penniless.

198
00:18:22.141 --> 00:18:24.018
I will not leave them fatherless as well.

199
00:18:24.101 --> 00:18:26.854
Small wonder Hightower vermin
swarm our streets

200
00:18:26.937 --> 00:18:29.774
when they smell your craven stink.

201
00:18:29.857 --> 00:18:32.652
My first duty must be to my family.

202
00:18:33.736 --> 00:18:36.238
I will earn our coin another way.

203
00:18:36.322 --> 00:18:38.783
And when cutthroats
and scoundrels swarm your house.

204
00:18:38.866 --> 00:18:43.287
rip the bread from your children's mouths.
and take their pleasure with your wife.

205
00:18:45.706 --> 00:18:46.999
All of you.

206
00:18:49.126 --> 00:18:51.045
You forget what this city was!

207
00:18:52.755 --> 00:18:55.675
Before I turned this rabble into an army.

208
00:18:55.758 --> 00:18:58.969
before I led you out of your squalor
and formed you into men!

209
00:19:02.682 --> 00:19:03.683
Shame.

210
00:19:35.423 --> 00:19:37.717
Word in the city is that
you've done valiant work.

211
00:19:38.884 --> 00:19:40.469
The Triarchy raids have dwindled.

212
00:19:42.096 --> 00:19:43.305
There's more to do.

213
00:19:44.974 --> 00:19:46.600
As ever will be the case.

214
00:19:48.436 --> 00:19:49.854
State your purpose. Alyn.

215
00:19:49.937 --> 00:19:53.232
Ormund Hightower strikes
insidiously at King's Landing.

216
00:19:53.315 --> 00:19:54.734
seeking to throw it into chaos.

217
00:19:55.735 --> 00:19:57.737
The City Watch is buckling.

218
00:19:57.820 --> 00:19:59.363
I would send to Driftmark

219
00:19:59.447 --> 00:20:01.240
to shore up their number
with good Velaryon men.

220
00:20:01.323 --> 00:20:03.409
So. she asks more of me.

221
00:20:05.536 --> 00:20:07.621
It is I who ask.

222
00:20:10.040 --> 00:20:13.002
Do as you have said.
Her needs are endless.

223
00:20:14.712 --> 00:20:17.256
Have you not exhausted your anger yet?

224
00:20:17.339 --> 00:20:18.841
You take her side...

225
00:20:19.925 --> 00:20:22.470
when she yet refuses
to grant you legitimacy.

226
00:20:22.553 --> 00:20:26.015
And how many years did it take you
to do the same?

227
00:20:32.146 --> 00:20:33.564
I have heard things...

228
00:20:35.441 --> 00:20:37.651
in questioning these pirates.

229
00:20:39.403 --> 00:20:41.947
Tell her Tyland Lannister
survived the Gullet...

230
00:20:43.866 --> 00:20:45.534
and is making for Rook's Rest.

231
00:21:03.886 --> 00:21:06.305
- That's enough.
- The dogs will find him.

232
00:21:07.598 --> 00:21:08.891
They're welcome to him.

233
00:21:08.974 --> 00:21:10.476
By the time they come. we'll be gone.

234
00:21:10.559 --> 00:21:12.561
But not far. And if the others realize--

235
00:21:12.645 --> 00:21:16.690
If you wish to dig deeper. Lord Larys.
the shovel is free.

236
00:21:27.743 --> 00:21:31.205
I have found passage to Braavos
on a merchant cog out of Maidenpool.

237
00:21:32.540 --> 00:21:35.376
We must draw as little notice
as we can for a few days

238
00:21:35.459 --> 00:21:37.211
as we provision ourselves. but...

239
00:21:39.171 --> 00:21:41.298
I believe we can sail
before the full moon.

240
00:21:42.299 --> 00:21:43.968
I must interject. my king.

241
00:21:45.135 --> 00:21:48.848
I still feel it would be an error
for you to leave Westeros.

242
00:21:50.432 --> 00:21:53.102
You would be best served at Casterly Rock.

243
00:21:53.185 --> 00:21:56.105
where we can establish a court
and enjoin those still loyal to you.

244
00:21:56.188 --> 00:22:00.234
Do you think I'm a terrible man.
Ser Tyland?

245
00:22:03.737 --> 00:22:05.030
I would never say...

246
00:22:06.323 --> 00:22:07.408
That is...

247
00:22:08.576 --> 00:22:11.203
while I may not have always agreed
with every course of...

248
00:22:13.414 --> 00:22:14.248
Well...

249
00:22:17.501 --> 00:22:18.502
There is...

250
00:22:19.837 --> 00:22:22.256
in any one of us. I venture...

251
00:22:23.382 --> 00:22:26.594
much to admire and much to be deplored.

252
00:22:36.687 --> 00:22:37.688
Mm.

253
00:22:40.232 --> 00:22:41.859
We sail for Essos. then.

254
00:23:27.529 --> 00:23:28.781
For your face.

255
00:23:35.496 --> 00:23:38.082
It's been long since anyone
sought to defend me.

256
00:23:40.167 --> 00:23:41.961
I am in your debt.

257
00:23:43.504 --> 00:23:45.130
As I am apparently in yours.

258
00:23:46.256 --> 00:23:48.968
But I'm glad I can leave here now
with that score settled.

259
00:23:52.054 --> 00:23:54.056
Where do you think to go?

260
00:23:54.139 --> 00:23:55.641
I need to find my dragon.

261
00:23:56.642 --> 00:24:00.521
She would not have left me willingly.
and I'll not be without her.

262
00:24:04.066 --> 00:24:06.318
A frog in winter sleeps under the ice.

263
00:24:07.277 --> 00:24:08.821
Still and silent.

264
00:24:10.698 --> 00:24:11.865
Mend your wounds.

265
00:24:13.117 --> 00:24:14.451
Gather your strength.

266
00:24:15.828 --> 00:24:20.082
Let the world think you dead
until the spring thaw.

267
00:24:21.875 --> 00:24:23.210
I need to find a horse.

268
00:24:24.211 --> 00:24:25.796
To ride where?

269
00:24:26.755 --> 00:24:28.590
Over the numberless leagues
of the Seven Kingdoms?

270
00:24:28.674 --> 00:24:30.467
Vhagar will come to me.

271
00:24:30.551 --> 00:24:33.095
It is perhaps this forsaken castle
she shuns.

272
00:24:33.178 --> 00:24:35.431
Or if not. I'll go to King's Landing.

273
00:24:36.473 --> 00:24:38.267
It's said she haunted
the hills outside the city

274
00:24:38.350 --> 00:24:40.019
in the years before I was born.

275
00:24:40.102 --> 00:24:41.937
There is a bounty on your life.

276
00:24:44.189 --> 00:24:49.361
Every sellsword is combing the woods
hoping to slit your throat in the night.

277
00:24:51.155 --> 00:24:52.948
Oh. and half the commonfolk. too.

278
00:24:55.826 --> 00:24:57.619
Even you must sleep.

279
00:24:59.663 --> 00:25:01.999
There's no place for you
to rest your head.

280
00:25:03.250 --> 00:25:04.877
And nor am I safe here then.

281
00:25:06.587 --> 00:25:08.964
Or you. for harboring me.

282
00:25:10.758 --> 00:25:15.888
Is it possible that Vhagar flew away
as a way of protecting you?

283
00:25:18.682 --> 00:25:20.309
Without her. you're hidden.

284
00:25:22.519 --> 00:25:25.105
The queen assumes that
where your dragon is...

285
00:25:27.191 --> 00:25:28.817
there you will be. too.

286
00:25:33.822 --> 00:25:35.491
She is no queen.

287
00:25:35.574 --> 00:25:39.411
And when you find your mount.
will you fly to your death?

288
00:25:41.246 --> 00:25:43.540
Rhaenyra has six dragons to your one.

289
00:25:44.833 --> 00:25:47.127
You'll fall alone.

290
00:25:47.211 --> 00:25:48.504
And to what end?

291
00:25:55.219 --> 00:25:56.929
Never ceases to be fascinating.

292
00:26:06.688 --> 00:26:08.148
As you ordered. my lady.

293
00:26:21.787 --> 00:26:23.497
What did I say. when last we met?

294
00:26:25.457 --> 00:26:26.875
I saw Moondancer...

295
00:26:28.085 --> 00:26:31.672
my sister's dragon.
flying towards Iron Oaks.

296
00:26:31.755 --> 00:26:33.257
And what does that to do with you?

297
00:26:34.258 --> 00:26:36.176
She's my sister. I...

298
00:26:37.261 --> 00:26:39.263
I thought if I could just see her face.

299
00:26:39.346 --> 00:26:42.724
So you leave your hiding place.
in violation of our agreement.

300
00:26:42.808 --> 00:26:46.228
and you fly toward a town equipped
with several thousand pairs of eyes.

301
00:26:46.311 --> 00:26:49.439
all watching and wondering
what your appearance portends.

302
00:26:49.523 --> 00:26:51.567
I didn't even see her.
She was already gone.

303
00:26:51.650 --> 00:26:53.777
And what do you think
would have happened if she hadn't?

304
00:26:57.322 --> 00:26:59.825
The queen thinks
Sheepstealer's rider is dead.

305
00:26:59.908 --> 00:27:02.911
It has been your only reprieve.
If word reaches her...

306
00:27:05.789 --> 00:27:08.333
Have you forgotten already
the doom that hangs over you?

307
00:27:11.003 --> 00:27:12.254
And over me.

308
00:27:13.797 --> 00:27:15.132
For harboring you.

309
00:27:16.967 --> 00:27:19.052
For allowing myself to be swayed.

310
00:27:20.387 --> 00:27:22.139
- I'm sorry.
- Mm.

311
00:27:22.681 --> 00:27:26.310
All my life.
I have yearned after a dragon.

312
00:27:28.520 --> 00:27:31.315
And now I have one.
but I have lost everything else.

313
00:27:33.567 --> 00:27:34.860
That was your choice.

314
00:27:36.111 --> 00:27:37.571
They are dead to you now.

315
00:27:38.655 --> 00:27:41.575
But you got what you wanted. Go.

316
00:27:42.826 --> 00:27:44.912
And the next time
you try me will be the last.

317
00:27:55.130 --> 00:27:56.882
A bed would be more comfortable.

318
00:27:59.551 --> 00:28:00.636
My lady.

319
00:28:02.763 --> 00:28:03.805
I'm going.

320
00:28:04.806 --> 00:28:06.892
I just needed a little more time.

321
00:28:06.975 --> 00:28:10.062
I know what it is to be so weary.

322
00:28:13.440 --> 00:28:14.900
I...

323
00:28:15.567 --> 00:28:17.027
saw my father today.

324
00:28:19.571 --> 00:28:21.573
I was wondering if you would speak to him.

325
00:28:24.076 --> 00:28:28.205
There is a distance there.
as if he's removed himself entirely.

326
00:28:29.581 --> 00:28:30.791
I just thought...

327
00:28:32.251 --> 00:28:35.295
maybe now he might...

328
00:28:37.256 --> 00:28:38.423
see me.

329
00:28:41.218 --> 00:28:42.803
I thought the same with my father.

330
00:28:44.763 --> 00:28:49.017
They cannot face their ghosts.
so they seek to outstrip them.

331
00:28:50.602 --> 00:28:52.229
Even if they leave us behind.

332
00:28:54.147 --> 00:28:58.568
They roam. they punish.
they fight. they do.

333
00:29:02.781 --> 00:29:04.199
I cannot help him. Alyn.

334
00:29:05.742 --> 00:29:07.828
I have my own burdens to bear.

335
00:29:22.718 --> 00:29:23.802
I...

336
00:29:24.469 --> 00:29:25.929
You should go to bed.

337
00:29:39.443 --> 00:29:40.902
You're very dutiful.

338
00:29:45.907 --> 00:29:47.200
I am the eldest.

339
00:29:49.494 --> 00:29:51.121
It must get wearisome...

340
00:29:52.539 --> 00:29:54.708
attending to everyone else all the time.

341
00:29:58.462 --> 00:29:59.796
Maybe a little.

342
00:30:02.883 --> 00:30:04.718
Don't you ever want to forget it all?

343
00:30:06.470 --> 00:30:07.971
Do what you want?

344
00:30:32.662 --> 00:30:37.793
And so. Ser Criston fights on.
and yet you have returned.

345
00:30:37.876 --> 00:30:38.877
Because...

346
00:30:40.212 --> 00:30:42.047
Because fighting on is madness.

347
00:30:45.842 --> 00:30:48.220
Do you think me mad. Your Grace?

348
00:30:48.303 --> 00:30:50.347
No. sire.

349
00:30:50.430 --> 00:30:51.431
Hm.

350
00:30:52.391 --> 00:30:53.767
You mean to fight on?

351
00:30:54.768 --> 00:30:56.561
With what?

352
00:30:56.645 --> 00:30:58.814
There's a dragon
sitting on the hill above us.

353
00:30:58.897 --> 00:31:00.607
and five more not 30 leagues away.

354
00:31:01.316 --> 00:31:03.777
Rhaenyra will not burn her own subjects.

355
00:31:03.860 --> 00:31:05.237
She is a woman.

356
00:31:06.405 --> 00:31:07.864
Squeamish.

357
00:31:07.948 --> 00:31:11.451
If your host leaves these walls. it burns.

358
00:31:13.161 --> 00:31:16.206
Aemond has fled
and Rhaenyra holds my sister hostage.

359
00:31:17.207 --> 00:31:19.251
The River army draws closer by the day.

360
00:31:19.334 --> 00:31:21.420
What possible course is there?

361
00:31:21.503 --> 00:31:24.381
Your uncle lacks imagination
as well as courage.

362
00:31:27.384 --> 00:31:31.304
I would take one Hightower sword
over three of Tully's mudmen.

363
00:31:33.682 --> 00:31:37.352
When the usurper's host comes here.
we will fight on our terms. on our ground.

364
00:31:40.355 --> 00:31:42.190
We have the clear advantage.

365
00:31:43.358 --> 00:31:47.154
Meanwhile. we are turning King's Landing
against that overweening cunt.

366
00:31:47.237 --> 00:31:49.739
little by little. bite by bite.

367
00:31:50.991 --> 00:31:53.702
Exposing her as weak and unsuited to rule.

368
00:31:55.203 --> 00:31:57.414
The great houses cannot
but come to our side.

369
00:31:58.498 --> 00:31:59.875
Have any yet come?

370
00:32:01.960 --> 00:32:04.754
The patient hunter gets the kill.

371
00:32:07.382 --> 00:32:09.926
Something the craven among us
would do well to learn.

372
00:32:12.220 --> 00:32:15.932
I have marched a long road.
fought and killed.

373
00:32:16.016 --> 00:32:18.685
and suffered my comrades
to be killed about me.

374
00:32:18.768 --> 00:32:20.312
Yes. you have endured much.

375
00:32:22.147 --> 00:32:26.026
I'm sure you found solace
with some of your brothers in arms.

376
00:32:27.110 --> 00:32:29.154
I am fatigued.

377
00:32:29.237 --> 00:32:31.573
It's been weeks
since I've seen a feather bed.

378
00:32:32.574 --> 00:32:34.201
By your leave.

379
00:32:34.284 --> 00:32:37.204
You might see Ser Gwayne
to his quarters. Your Grace.

380
00:32:37.287 --> 00:32:38.788
Make sure he bathes.

381
00:32:43.960 --> 00:32:45.670
Oh. and...

382
00:32:47.005 --> 00:32:48.298
Mind yourself.

383
00:32:49.132 --> 00:32:51.051
Backs against the wall.

384
00:32:54.471 --> 00:32:57.265
- "Your Grace"?
- I'm sorry. I had to get through it.

385
00:32:57.349 --> 00:32:59.809
And this is your way? Fawning?

386
00:32:59.893 --> 00:33:01.228
Daeron.

387
00:33:01.311 --> 00:33:03.313
He's styled you the bloody king.

388
00:33:03.396 --> 00:33:04.898
You left me alone with him.

389
00:33:05.649 --> 00:33:07.108
You know what he is.

390
00:33:07.192 --> 00:33:08.860
I do what I can to keep him from...

391
00:33:10.070 --> 00:33:11.071
you know.

392
00:33:12.072 --> 00:33:13.698
I had no choice.

393
00:33:13.782 --> 00:33:15.200
No.

394
00:33:15.283 --> 00:33:17.494
But neither did it grieve you
to ride away.

395
00:33:21.122 --> 00:33:23.667
I hate what I am when I'm with him.

396
00:33:23.750 --> 00:33:26.711
A puppet. a fool. a child.

397
00:33:26.795 --> 00:33:29.339
And yet he means to put you
on the throne. apparently.

398
00:33:30.632 --> 00:33:33.051
Only as he cannot sit on it himself.

399
00:33:33.134 --> 00:33:35.720
No. he would thrust me forward
and devour me from within

400
00:33:35.804 --> 00:33:37.389
until there's nothing left.

401
00:33:37.472 --> 00:33:39.599
So tell him you won't do it.

402
00:33:39.683 --> 00:33:41.184
Then who will protect me then?

403
00:33:42.519 --> 00:33:45.313
Will you raise an army
against his savages?

404
00:33:48.692 --> 00:33:51.653
If you were king. you could cast him down.

405
00:33:51.736 --> 00:33:54.364
I will never be king. uncle.
we both know it.

406
00:33:56.908 --> 00:33:58.410
I need to lie down.

407
00:33:58.493 --> 00:34:00.537
- You'll stay. won't you?
- And do what?

408
00:34:01.830 --> 00:34:05.250
Bear witness whilst Ormund
marches our house to its doom?

409
00:34:07.043 --> 00:34:09.796
I'm second in line.
I shall return to Oldtown

410
00:34:09.879 --> 00:34:11.715
and prepare to pick up the pieces.

411
00:34:11.798 --> 00:34:14.968
Don't leave me again. Please.

412
00:34:15.051 --> 00:34:18.722
You're his little treasure now.
You'll be fine.

413
00:34:21.224 --> 00:34:23.143
When you were in King's Landing...

414
00:34:28.189 --> 00:34:29.733
Did you see my mother?

415
00:34:34.654 --> 00:34:36.364
Will you not eat?

416
00:34:40.452 --> 00:34:43.663
You have taken nothing since yesterday
and said little more.

417
00:34:50.629 --> 00:34:51.880
Helaena.

418
00:34:54.966 --> 00:34:59.179
Mysaria knew of our plan.
but she said nothing of Jaehaera.

419
00:35:01.306 --> 00:35:03.808
Was she truly stolen away to meet us

420
00:35:03.892 --> 00:35:06.895
at some secret place up ahead?

421
00:35:13.401 --> 00:35:14.569
I see.

422
00:35:17.197 --> 00:35:18.782
Forgive me. Helaena.

423
00:35:18.865 --> 00:35:22.202
The road ahead was fraught with peril.

424
00:35:22.285 --> 00:35:23.787
- To bring a small child--
- You lied.

425
00:35:26.623 --> 00:35:28.750
I wished only to save you from this place.

426
00:35:29.751 --> 00:35:30.919
Me?

427
00:35:32.504 --> 00:35:33.797
Or yourself?

428
00:35:36.466 --> 00:35:38.093
What difference does it make?

429
00:35:40.428 --> 00:35:43.890
I have come too far.
I have sacrificed too much.

430
00:35:45.600 --> 00:35:47.936
If I cannot at long last
salvage my daughter...

431
00:35:57.821 --> 00:35:59.280
Helaena. please.

432
00:36:01.783 --> 00:36:03.952
Please. you must eat.

433
00:36:37.777 --> 00:36:38.903
One-Eye.

434
00:36:48.455 --> 00:36:49.873
I have kept your secret.

435
00:36:51.082 --> 00:36:52.751
I will keep it still.

436
00:36:52.834 --> 00:36:54.461
You could have killed me. too.

437
00:36:55.587 --> 00:36:56.921
And claimed Rhaenyra's bounty.

438
00:36:58.131 --> 00:37:00.175
There are many things
I could have done to you.

439
00:37:02.051 --> 00:37:03.887
Then what is this game you play?

440
00:37:05.555 --> 00:37:07.015
It's yours to learn.

441
00:37:08.433 --> 00:37:10.059
If your spirit is willing.

442
00:37:29.621 --> 00:37:31.372
Have you forgotten your history?

443
00:37:33.041 --> 00:37:34.501
Dreamfyre.

444
00:37:34.584 --> 00:37:36.961
Your ancestor

445
00:37:37.045 --> 00:37:41.049
Rhaena Targaryen came to Harrenhal
after the death of her daughter.

446
00:37:42.258 --> 00:37:45.136
And she grieved and grew old here.

447
00:37:46.137 --> 00:37:48.932
Her dragon laid a clutch of eggs
before Rhaena herself died.

448
00:37:49.015 --> 00:37:53.645
and they have sat here.
cold and abandoned these hundred years.

449
00:37:55.396 --> 00:37:57.273
I do not know the ways of dragons.

450
00:37:57.357 --> 00:38:01.069
but I have long envisaged
the return of the Targaryens

451
00:38:01.152 --> 00:38:03.613
to this ancient seat.

452
00:38:10.829 --> 00:38:12.622
I have been cursed for my sins...

453
00:38:13.790 --> 00:38:14.874
Alys.

454
00:38:16.459 --> 00:38:19.087
All I put my hand to
withers beneath its touch.

455
00:38:20.380 --> 00:38:24.259
Do you imagine that you alone
know what it is to be cursed?

456
00:38:27.637 --> 00:38:30.682
I'm tired of this desolate existence.

457
00:38:32.517 --> 00:38:34.519
And so. I think. are you.

458
00:38:38.398 --> 00:38:41.109
You've been alone your whole life. Aemond.

459
00:38:43.361 --> 00:38:45.572
Can you not imagine...

460
00:38:46.865 --> 00:38:48.283
what it would be...

461
00:38:49.951 --> 00:38:52.203
to have it otherwise?

462
00:39:00.295 --> 00:39:01.713
It's warm.

463
00:39:07.218 --> 00:39:09.429
There's an ancient strength here.

464
00:39:11.180 --> 00:39:13.474
Let the gods turn their backs on us.

465
00:39:13.558 --> 00:39:15.810
We will make our own fortune.

466
00:39:18.771 --> 00:39:20.690
I will be the Lady of the Water.

467
00:39:23.484 --> 00:39:24.736
And you...

468
00:39:27.238 --> 00:39:30.909
the dragonlord by my side.

469
00:39:35.663 --> 00:39:38.416
But in the meantime.
you're a Targaryen prince.

470
00:39:40.710 --> 00:39:42.921
And your sons

471
00:39:43.004 --> 00:39:46.758
will be Targaryen princes in their turn.

472
00:39:56.726 --> 00:39:59.228
Tallow is scarce
and cost thrice what it did.

473
00:39:59.312 --> 00:40:00.939
We cannot light our sconces.

474
00:40:01.022 --> 00:40:02.482
You know my response.

475
00:40:02.565 --> 00:40:04.901
Ser Torrhen Manderly is Master of Coin.

476
00:40:04.984 --> 00:40:08.112
It is his task now to distribute
what resources we have.

477
00:40:09.072 --> 00:40:11.366
I suggest you address Ser Torrhen himself.

478
00:40:12.533 --> 00:40:13.952
Bring the next.

479
00:40:15.578 --> 00:40:17.622
Your Grace.

480
00:40:17.705 --> 00:40:20.959
The motherhouse
lately enjoyed the protection

481
00:40:21.042 --> 00:40:22.752
of the City Watch.

482
00:40:24.003 --> 00:40:26.089
Now. we are in peril.

483
00:40:27.006 --> 00:40:31.302
One of our girls
only last night was taken.

484
00:40:32.303 --> 00:40:34.305
You have my condolences. I shall...

485
00:40:36.391 --> 00:40:39.018
light a candle for her
when next I attend the sept.

486
00:40:42.772 --> 00:40:45.108
Godric. Your Grace. A mason.

487
00:40:45.191 --> 00:40:47.944
We have watched in fear
as we found gold cloaks murdered among us.

488
00:40:48.027 --> 00:40:51.447
and I have heard a great number of 'em
have resigned their posts.

489
00:40:51.531 --> 00:40:52.949
leaving the streets undefended.

490
00:40:53.032 --> 00:40:54.993
Yes. these are Hightower crimes.

491
00:40:55.952 --> 00:40:58.121
The craven Ormund strikes at me
from Tumbleton.

492
00:40:58.204 --> 00:41:00.957
where he has concealed himself
among innocents.

493
00:41:01.040 --> 00:41:02.125
This we know.

494
00:41:02.208 --> 00:41:03.918
But how will we now be protected?

495
00:41:04.002 --> 00:41:06.587
If the City Watch fails.
then who will preserve order among us?

496
00:41:06.671 --> 00:41:08.548
I have sent for Velaryon men

497
00:41:08.631 --> 00:41:10.591
to root out the enemy within our walls.

498
00:41:10.675 --> 00:41:12.218
Once they arrive.
the city shall be returned--

499
00:41:12.301 --> 00:41:13.928
How will they be protected?

500
00:41:14.012 --> 00:41:16.681
She was but six and 10!

501
00:41:18.850 --> 00:41:21.519
Your Grace. we are afraid.

502
00:41:21.602 --> 00:41:25.648
And wherever the fault lies.
we have none to look to now but you.

503
00:42:28.294 --> 00:42:29.629
Daemon Targaryen.

504
00:42:31.047 --> 00:42:32.840
How many?

505
00:42:32.924 --> 00:42:34.801
How many of you are there?

506
00:42:35.676 --> 00:42:38.221
- How many?!
- We have no number.

507
00:42:38.304 --> 00:42:40.098
We are everywhere.

508
00:42:43.768 --> 00:42:45.603
What did Ormund Hightower
promise you. gold?

509
00:42:45.686 --> 00:42:46.896
Huh?

510
00:42:46.979 --> 00:42:48.773
A place at his table
when he takes the throne?

511
00:42:48.856 --> 00:42:52.068
There is a king
waiting just outside these walls.

512
00:42:52.151 --> 00:42:54.237
And until Daeron the Daring
takes his rightful place.

513
00:42:54.320 --> 00:42:55.738
we will not rest.

514
00:42:55.822 --> 00:43:00.076
Then your kind will die in dragonfire.
or trampled down by my army.

515
00:43:00.952 --> 00:43:03.246
Will she lay waste to her own city?

516
00:43:03.329 --> 00:43:05.748
Will she set upon her own people
with swords?

517
00:43:05.832 --> 00:43:06.999
You'll never find us.

518
00:43:07.083 --> 00:43:08.543
We're the people of the Seven Kingdoms.

519
00:43:08.626 --> 00:43:10.294
We have no sign or sigil.

520
00:43:10.378 --> 00:43:11.796
And when you strike us.

521
00:43:11.879 --> 00:43:14.715
you only drive more to our cause.

522
00:43:16.676 --> 00:43:20.179
You rebel against one
who has neither wished nor done you harm.

523
00:43:21.222 --> 00:43:24.100
You can burn us. You can kill us.

524
00:43:24.183 --> 00:43:26.102
You will never make us embrace her.

525
00:43:47.123 --> 00:43:48.207
Watch where you're fucking...

526
00:43:49.834 --> 00:43:50.960
Your prince.

527
00:43:52.295 --> 00:43:53.129
Your Grace.

528
00:43:54.130 --> 00:43:55.673
What is your errand here?

529
00:43:55.756 --> 00:43:58.092
I-- I was-- I thought...

530
00:43:59.093 --> 00:44:00.469
I...

531
00:44:00.553 --> 00:44:01.679
I was just...

532
00:44:02.221 --> 00:44:03.639
I'm taking the air.

533
00:44:03.723 --> 00:44:06.267
Are you not commanded to stay
in the Keep under guard?

534
00:44:08.936 --> 00:44:10.062
Well. yes.

535
00:44:11.439 --> 00:44:13.566
In a manner of speaking.

536
00:44:13.649 --> 00:44:15.026
Insolent maggot.

537
00:44:15.860 --> 00:44:18.446
I'm up that bloody hill
for days at a time.

538
00:44:19.572 --> 00:44:21.532
Men deserve their simple pleasures.

539
00:44:22.867 --> 00:44:24.243
Keep us going.

540
00:44:25.453 --> 00:44:27.079
You yourself should understand--

541
00:44:32.168 --> 00:44:33.669
Set foot in the city again.

542
00:44:33.753 --> 00:44:35.630
and I'll put out your eyes.

543
00:45:22.677 --> 00:45:24.220
Ho. there.

544
00:45:25.054 --> 00:45:26.806
Ho. Friend.

545
00:45:34.730 --> 00:45:37.316
Come on! Put your backs into it!

546
00:45:39.860 --> 00:45:41.112
Come on!

547
00:45:44.740 --> 00:45:45.741
All clear!

548
00:45:47.451 --> 00:45:48.786
Here.

549
00:45:59.755 --> 00:46:03.551
<i>The common man is. as a rule.</i>
<i>of no interest or concern.</i>

550
00:46:03.634 --> 00:46:07.221
<i>But you must never trust one</i>
<i>who's clawed his way to power.</i>

551
00:46:07.305 --> 00:46:10.474
His ambition is oft fueled by some lack.

552
00:46:11.392 --> 00:46:14.770
Some shame. or lust. or rage.

553
00:46:16.605 --> 00:46:17.898
Mm.

554
00:46:17.982 --> 00:46:20.359
You should think on it
when you choose your Hand.

555
00:46:20.443 --> 00:46:23.446
Rhaenyra made a rare good choice
with Corlys Velaryon.

556
00:46:24.405 --> 00:46:26.532
There is a soundness to his breeding.

557
00:46:26.615 --> 00:46:29.201
Not the sordid appetite of the striver.

558
00:46:30.494 --> 00:46:31.871
What of my grandsire?

559
00:46:33.414 --> 00:46:34.999
Otto?

560
00:46:35.082 --> 00:46:36.625
Where do I begin?

561
00:46:36.709 --> 00:46:41.380
My lord. House Baratheon sends an envoy
to treat with the new king.

562
00:46:43.591 --> 00:46:46.052
Let the Stormlands lead the way.

563
00:46:46.135 --> 00:46:48.179
Highgarden will have no choice
but to follow.

564
00:46:49.680 --> 00:46:51.390
Ah. Stand up.

565
00:46:51.474 --> 00:46:52.683
Stand up. both of you!

566
00:46:55.144 --> 00:46:58.898
Lord Ormund Hightower.
Beacon of the South.

567
00:46:58.981 --> 00:47:03.986
Defender of the Citadel.
and Voice of Oldtown.

568
00:47:07.198 --> 00:47:08.783
Well met. Ser Ormund.

569
00:47:09.700 --> 00:47:12.328
I come as an envoy
of Lord Borros Baratheon.

570
00:47:12.411 --> 00:47:14.580
Lord Paramount of the Stormlands.

571
00:47:19.335 --> 00:47:22.630
- You are quite welcome. Ser...
- Ser Arrion Baratheon.

572
00:47:22.713 --> 00:47:24.673
Cousin to Lord Borros.

573
00:47:28.928 --> 00:47:31.889
I most regret presenting
ourselves to you in this state.

574
00:47:31.972 --> 00:47:33.849
The road was long and filthy.

575
00:47:33.933 --> 00:47:36.477
but I thought it best
to speak to you immediately.

576
00:47:36.560 --> 00:47:37.770
We are honored to receive you.

577
00:47:38.771 --> 00:47:40.773
And what word from Lord Borros?

578
00:47:40.856 --> 00:47:43.275
Well. House Baratheon
bends the knee to His Grace.

579
00:47:43.359 --> 00:47:45.820
King Daeron Targaryen.
and offers its many banners

580
00:47:45.903 --> 00:47:47.655
in alliance with House Hightower.

581
00:47:49.740 --> 00:47:51.742
I have been ordered to swear fealty

582
00:47:51.826 --> 00:47:54.036
to the new king on behalf of Lord Borros.

583
00:47:55.746 --> 00:47:58.249
Your lord has made a wise choice.

584
00:48:01.460 --> 00:48:05.506
If we might see the king in person.
that we may bend the knee before him.

585
00:48:08.884 --> 00:48:11.470
His Grace. Daeron Targaryen.

586
00:48:13.681 --> 00:48:15.141
The First of his Name.

587
00:48:17.184 --> 00:48:20.062
King of the Andals. the Rhoynar and the--

588
00:48:21.230 --> 00:48:22.481
No! Stop him!

589
00:48:22.565 --> 00:48:23.858
Stop him!

590
00:48:23.941 --> 00:48:25.276
- Stop him!
- No!

591
00:48:26.694 --> 00:48:30.322
These are assassins.
sent for Daeron and you.

592
00:48:45.629 --> 00:48:49.633
Ser Arrion Baratheon
has hair of light chestnut.

593
00:48:49.717 --> 00:48:52.511
He's about a foot taller.
and as it happens...

594
00:48:53.429 --> 00:48:54.388
far more comely.

595
00:48:59.185 --> 00:49:02.396
I will cleave the bitch
from crown to cunt.

596
00:49:03.397 --> 00:49:05.441
She will die wishing she never dared...

597
00:49:07.735 --> 00:49:08.777
Dared...

598
00:49:19.538 --> 00:49:20.539
Kat.

599
00:49:34.678 --> 00:49:36.722
I thought you were dead.

600
00:49:50.277 --> 00:49:52.112
I looked for you.

601
00:49:52.196 --> 00:49:53.989
I went home. but you'd gone.

602
00:49:54.073 --> 00:49:55.950
What choice did I have?

603
00:49:57.535 --> 00:49:58.744
I was alone.

604
00:50:00.204 --> 00:50:03.165
I escaped in the chaos.
I came here to my brother.

605
00:50:04.166 --> 00:50:05.751
And now. he's dead. too.

606
00:50:08.420 --> 00:50:10.089
But Kat. I've done it.

607
00:50:11.090 --> 00:50:12.716
I claimed a dragon.

608
00:50:13.634 --> 00:50:15.803
Vermithor. the Bronze Fury.

609
00:50:15.886 --> 00:50:17.555
I've been made a knight.

610
00:50:18.681 --> 00:50:20.516
And the queen has promised--

611
00:50:25.062 --> 00:50:26.647
Is that what this is?

612
00:50:28.065 --> 00:50:29.650
Dragon?

613
00:50:32.361 --> 00:50:35.114
- You smell different.
- We'll have coin now.

614
00:50:35.197 --> 00:50:37.032
A fine house. anything you wish.

615
00:50:37.950 --> 00:50:40.119
I can take you out of this to safety.

616
00:50:40.202 --> 00:50:41.453
Do you not see?

617
00:50:41.537 --> 00:50:44.164
Your husband is a dragonrider.

618
00:50:45.249 --> 00:50:46.959
Do you know how many days it takes...

619
00:50:48.252 --> 00:50:50.588
to walk the road here from King's Landing?

620
00:50:53.424 --> 00:50:57.469
Do you know what may befall
a woman alone on that road?

621
00:50:58.012 --> 00:50:59.680
Did something happen?

622
00:51:01.307 --> 00:51:02.933
Many things happened.

623
00:51:05.102 --> 00:51:08.522
While you were on Dragonstone...

624
00:51:09.481 --> 00:51:11.775
- seeking out your own glory.
- I did it for you.

625
00:51:11.859 --> 00:51:13.319
I didn't want it!

626
00:51:15.237 --> 00:51:18.449
I needed you here.

627
00:51:19.575 --> 00:51:21.160
On the ground.

628
00:51:25.831 --> 00:51:27.916
I'm sorry. I am.

629
00:51:28.000 --> 00:51:29.877
But I can stay no longer.

630
00:51:29.960 --> 00:51:31.670
If I am discovered here...

631
00:51:31.754 --> 00:51:33.339
Just come with me.

632
00:51:34.632 --> 00:51:36.550
I won't forsake my family.

633
00:51:38.844 --> 00:51:40.179
There is no time. Come. we're going.

634
00:51:40.262 --> 00:51:42.765
- No!
- I will not leave you in peril.

635
00:51:42.848 --> 00:51:44.099
What are you doing?

636
00:51:46.977 --> 00:51:48.187
Who are you?!

637
00:52:20.094 --> 00:52:21.720
You did well.

638
00:52:22.388 --> 00:52:25.099
I treated you harshly.
and for that. I'm sorry.

639
00:52:26.517 --> 00:52:28.352
The strains of the campaign.

640
00:52:32.064 --> 00:52:34.775
You may return to Oldtown if you wish.

641
00:52:34.858 --> 00:52:37.194
A small band of men won't attract
the attention of the dragons.

642
00:52:38.696 --> 00:52:40.531
- I'll not stop you.
- There are three of you.

643
00:52:40.614 --> 00:52:42.741
Should be easy. Again.

644
00:52:44.868 --> 00:52:46.412
He'd make a good king.

645
00:52:48.414 --> 00:52:49.998
Not that that matters to you.

646
00:52:54.253 --> 00:52:56.714
You think me so callous.

647
00:52:57.673 --> 00:53:01.051
I think you'd sacrifice lives
to feed your own pride.

648
00:53:03.679 --> 00:53:05.889
But I know you'd never sacrifice your own.

649
00:53:09.184 --> 00:53:10.436
So. tell me.

650
00:53:12.646 --> 00:53:14.022
What is your plan here?

651
00:53:18.110 --> 00:53:19.528
Speak your purpose.

652
00:53:21.196 --> 00:53:22.197
Helaena.

653
00:53:23.365 --> 00:53:24.825
She cannot stay confined.

654
00:53:26.243 --> 00:53:28.954
Her state of mind is precarious.
her condition being what it is.

655
00:53:29.037 --> 00:53:31.623
Do you have something useful for me.
or have I been misled?

656
00:53:35.002 --> 00:53:36.462
I know where Aemond is.

657
00:53:39.298 --> 00:53:41.884
- All this time?
- Only lately.

658
00:53:44.803 --> 00:53:47.264
I would need a guarantee
that we'd go free.

659
00:53:48.140 --> 00:53:49.516
Both of us. as originally agreed.

660
00:53:49.600 --> 00:53:52.352
You're in no place to demand
guarantees of anything.

661
00:53:52.436 --> 00:53:54.480
When Aemond is gone.
your reign is assured.

662
00:53:55.981 --> 00:53:57.149
Ormund will surrender or die.

663
00:53:57.232 --> 00:53:58.734
Helaena and I are no threat to you.

664
00:53:58.817 --> 00:54:01.028
We will disappear.
You will not hear of us again.

665
00:54:07.117 --> 00:54:08.660
Where is he?

666
00:54:09.787 --> 00:54:10.871
Harrenhal.

667
00:54:11.997 --> 00:54:14.500
My riders have searched for Vhagar there

668
00:54:14.583 --> 00:54:17.419
- half a dozen times.
- I did not say I know where Vhagar is.

669
00:54:21.006 --> 00:54:22.674
How did you come by this?

670
00:54:24.593 --> 00:54:26.053
There are times when Helaena...

671
00:54:27.012 --> 00:54:28.555
when Helaena sees things.

672
00:54:29.473 --> 00:54:31.183
It will sound mad.

673
00:54:31.266 --> 00:54:33.811
They are nightmares or puzzles.

674
00:54:35.979 --> 00:54:38.774
But the things she does see now and then.
they come to pass.

675
00:54:41.026 --> 00:54:42.486
She dreams.

676
00:54:44.613 --> 00:54:46.281
She's a dreamer.

677
00:54:48.075 --> 00:54:49.785
Like Daenys who foresaw the Doom.

678
00:54:56.166 --> 00:54:58.252
If what you say is true.

679
00:54:58.335 --> 00:55:01.630
if Aemond has separated
somehow from his dragon...

680
00:55:03.549 --> 00:55:04.675
then...

681
00:55:06.218 --> 00:55:08.345
he is one man on foot...

682
00:55:09.847 --> 00:55:11.181
and being hunted.

683
00:55:13.433 --> 00:55:15.519
He will have hidden himself
so he cannot be found.

684
00:55:15.602 --> 00:55:17.020
I have told you all that I know.

685
00:55:17.104 --> 00:55:19.523
His capture must now
fall to you and your council.

686
00:55:19.606 --> 00:55:20.607
No.

687
00:55:24.778 --> 00:55:27.239
If I send swords...

688
00:55:29.366 --> 00:55:31.285
he will flee again. go to ground.

689
00:55:31.368 --> 00:55:32.661
and be lost. but...

690
00:55:38.417 --> 00:55:40.043
If I send just one sword...

691
00:55:45.924 --> 00:55:47.718
with someone he trusts...

692
00:55:56.101 --> 00:55:57.811
No. I will be no part of this.

693
00:56:00.188 --> 00:56:03.483
- No. please. Rhaenyra.
- Unhand her Grace.

694
00:56:07.404 --> 00:56:08.405
I...

695
00:56:09.406 --> 00:56:10.657
I...

696
00:56:10.741 --> 00:56:12.451
I cannot leave Helaena.

697
00:56:18.790 --> 00:56:20.292
I will keep watch over her.

698
00:56:21.543 --> 00:56:22.961
Until you return.

699
00:56:28.926 --> 00:56:30.218
Did I not warn you...

700
00:56:31.637 --> 00:56:33.055
that you would come to this?

701
00:56:53.867 --> 00:56:55.410
I don't want to be alone.

702
00:56:58.205 --> 00:56:59.456
Nor do I.

703
00:57:01.291 --> 00:57:02.542
I have no choice.

704
00:57:07.172 --> 00:57:08.173
Here.

705
00:57:09.466 --> 00:57:11.176
You could refuse.

706
00:57:15.222 --> 00:57:16.932
And Aemond would still be like to die.

707
00:57:19.059 --> 00:57:21.103
Do you not wish to be free?

708
00:57:24.398 --> 00:57:25.774
Why am I here?

709
00:57:29.194 --> 00:57:31.738
Was there no other lord
that offered for my hand?

710
00:57:35.575 --> 00:57:41.498
Or was it your own desire
to marry me to my brother?

711
00:57:48.797 --> 00:57:50.424
It was my father's wish.

712
00:57:53.427 --> 00:57:54.970
But I did not begrudge it.

713
00:57:57.472 --> 00:58:01.435
Better here with me. I thought.
than a man you did not know

714
00:58:01.518 --> 00:58:03.895
in a place far away.

715
00:58:13.488 --> 00:58:15.949
Please. Please.

716
00:58:19.453 --> 00:58:23.623
We still have some
small chance at freedom. Helaena.

717
00:58:25.500 --> 00:58:27.836
But I cannot go unless I know
you are sustained.

718
00:58:31.298 --> 00:58:32.299
Please.

719
00:58:46.021 --> 00:58:47.272
There.

720
00:58:50.317 --> 00:58:53.653
I will return to you as soon as I am able.

721
00:58:53.737 --> 00:58:55.489
I give you my word.

722
00:58:55.572 --> 00:58:58.366
I will come back and collect you.
and we will...

723
00:58:59.284 --> 00:59:01.203
we will walk out in the sun.

724
00:59:30.023 --> 00:59:31.775
Forgive the hour. Your Grace.

725
00:59:34.611 --> 00:59:38.532
There has been a rider from Tumbleton.

726
00:59:47.124 --> 00:59:48.750
"Kick this dog...

727
00:59:49.876 --> 00:59:52.087
and it will bite your hand."

728
00:59:59.594 --> 01:00:02.430
<i>You have fought like sharks.</i>

729
01:00:03.765 --> 01:00:06.059
<i>Swift and relentless.</i>

730
01:00:07.644 --> 01:00:12.941
We have cut through our enemy
and routed them!

731
01:00:14.609 --> 01:00:18.196
But now. your blades
are needed in the city.

732
01:00:21.783 --> 01:00:23.076
And I...

733
01:00:24.703 --> 01:00:26.496
I have been too long away.

734
01:00:39.926 --> 01:00:41.094
Who are you?

735
01:00:42.512 --> 01:00:44.055
What's your errand?

735
01:00:45.305 --> 01:01:45.638
